signal.description:
Emitted when a server bullet hits a physics body. [param bullet] is the [code]_TamaServerBullet[/code] wrapper for the bullet that made contact. [param body_instance_id] is the [method Object.get_instance_id] of the body that was hit — use [method @GlobalScope.instance_from_id] to retrieve the node.

[codeblock]
func _ready():
    TamaManager.bullet_hit.connect(_on_bullet_hit)

func _on_bullet_hit(bullet, body_instance_id: int) -> void:
    if body_instance_id == get_instance_id():
        pass  # this node was hit
[/codeblock]

[b]Note:[/b] This signal is only emitted for server bullets (registered with [method register_server_bullet]). Scene bullets use normal Godot [Area2D] collision signals.
